+| `223_array_row_drops` | elements with destructors inside heap blocks of rows dropped exactly once; `rows_host_throw` is the host-throw path |
+| `224_flattened_pointers` | pointers into rows and into their flattened view: one place under `ptr::eq` and the pointer order, one address under `as usize`, for stack rows, a `Vec` and a `Box<[T; N]>` |
+| `225_array_row_shapes` | by-value iteration of rows, `drain`/`split_off`/`append`/`dedup`/`resize`, `Rc` of rows, rows not written yet, and rows of rows on the heap |
 | `guard_as_chunks` | a gap that is a run time guard rather than a zombie: `as_chunks` aborts the program instead of answering |
 | `guard_heap_retype` | reading one heap block at two element sizes once something has been written at the first: `__rt.unscale` throws rather than hand back a wrong number |
